## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical CSS skills: grid/flex, CSS-only interactivity, and accessible animation. Demonstrates how to implement a scalable gallery with keyboard focus and motion preferences.

## Key Concepts

- CSS Grid responsive columns
- Flexbox caption alignment
- CSS-only state toggling (checkbox hack)
- Entrance stagger and per-item delay
- Accessibility: focus-visible, prefers-reduced-motion

## Code Example

```css
.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px}
@media (max-width:1024px){.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
@media (max-width:600px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.card{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.caption{transform:translateY(8px);opacity:.0;transition:.25s}
#captions:checked ~ .grid .caption{transform:none;opacity:1}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){.grid,.caption{transition:none}}
```

```html
<input type="checkbox" id="captions" />
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card" tabindex="0">
    <img src="image.jpg" alt="Sample" />
    <div class="caption">Sample</div>
  </div>
</div>
```

