## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to pair dynamic imports with route-driven loading and Lighthouse budgets in a concrete, beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Route-based code-splitting
- Lighthouse budget enforcement
- Lazy-loading non-critical assets

## Code Example
```javascript
// minimal sketch
import React, {Suspense, useState} from 'react';
const AnalyticsPanel = React.lazy(() => import('./AnalyticsPanel'));

function App() {
  const [route, setRoute] = useState('/');
  return (
    <div>
      {route === '/analytics' ? (
        <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading…</div>}>
          <AnalyticsPanel />
        </Suspense>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}
```

