- How would you validate LCP under 2.5s across devices?
- How would you extend to prefetch the panel when hovering the Analytics tab?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to integrate fetch, WebSocket, and Service Worker workflows in a realistic UI pattern. It emphasizes error handling, reconnection strategies, offline behavior, and efficient DOM updates—critical in production frontend apps.

Key Concepts
- Fetch with AbortController: timeout and robust error handling
- WebSocket lifecycle: onopen/onmessage/onclose, exponential backoff reconnect
- Service Worker: caching shell and API responses; offline/online transitions
- Offline queue: persisting submissions (IndexedDB) and retry logic
- DOM rendering: debounced updates to minimize reflows

Code Example
```javascript
async function loadComments(productId){
  const ac = new AbortController();
  const timer = setTimeout(() => ac.abort(), 5000);
  try{
    const res = await fetch(`/api/comments?productId=${productId}`, {signal: ac.signal});
    if(!res.ok) throw new Error(res.status);
    return await res.json();
  } catch(e){
    return [];
  } finally{ clearTimeout(timer); }
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you test offline queue persistence across page reloads?
- How would you handle WebSocket backoff in fluctuating networks?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply real-world performance constraints to modern frontends, focusing on Lighthouse budgets, code-splitting, lazy loading, and runtime scheduling with production instrumentation and feature-flag parity.

## Key Concepts

- Progressive hydration
- Code splitting and dynamic imports
- Idle-time scheduling (requestIdleCallback, Scheduler)
- Lighthouse budget enforcement in CI
- Feature flags for parity verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// loadAfterInteract.js
export function loadAfterInteract(importFn) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const tryLoad = () => {
      const p = importFn();
      Promise.resolve(p).then(resolve, reject);
    };
    if ('requestIdleCallback' in window) {
      requestIdleCallback(tryLoad, { timeout: 1000 });
    } else {
      setTimeout(tryLoad, 0);
    }
  });
}
```

```javascript
// budgetRunner.js
let budgetActive = true;
export function runWithBudget(task, limitMs = 60) {
  const t0 = performance.now();
  task();
  const dt = performance.now() - t0;
  if (dt > limitMs) budgetActive = false;
}
```

